+# Bug Assessment: Product deletion breaks carts and historical orders
+
+- **Slug**: ticket
+- **Created**: 2026-11-18T00:00:00+00:00
+- **Source**: pasted text
+- **Verdict**: valid
+- **Severity**: high
+
+## Report (verbatim or summarized)
+
+Deleting a product through `DELETE /api/v1/private/product/{id}` currently breaks carts and orders containing it. The requested behavior is to remove deleted products from carts while preserving usable carts and recalculated totals, reject future additions with 404, preserve order snapshots and totals after deletion across private/customer order APIs, keep checkout and status updates working, return 404 for deleted product lookup, and leave unrelated products unaffected.
+
+## Symptom
+
+After a product is deleted, a cart or order that references its SKU can no longer be read or checked out. Expected behavior is that cart line items for the deleted product disappear and cart totals are recalculated, while order lines continue to expose their persisted SKU, name, quantity, price, and subtotal.
+
+## Reproduction
+
+1. Create a product, add it to a cart, and create an order containing it.
+2. Delete the product with `DELETE /api/v1/private/product/{id}`.
+3. Read the cart, modify or check it out, read the order through private and authenticated endpoints, update order status, and look up the deleted SKU through `GET /api/v2/product/{sku}`.
+4. Verify that the deleted cart item is absent and totals use remaining products, historical order data is unchanged, deleted-product additions/lookups return 404, and other products remain usable.
+
+## Suspected Code Paths
+
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/facade/product/ProductCommonFacadeImpl.java:388-410` — product deletion physically removes the catalog product and its dependent catalog data.
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/shoppingcart/ShoppingCartServiceImpl.java:184-270` — cart loading resolves each persisted SKU; missing products are marked obsolete, and any obsolete item currently marks the entire cart obsolete and causes deletion.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/mapper/cart/ReadableShoppingCartMapper.java:128-287` — cart mapping dereferences `item.getProduct()` and calculates response totals/quantity from line items.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/shoppingCart/facade/ShoppingCartFacadeImpl.java:250-330` — cart additions resolve products by SKU and currently throw a generic exception for missing products.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/mapper/order/ReadableOrderProductMapper.java:45-125` and `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/populator/order/ReadableOrderProductPopulator.java:45-125` — historical order fields are persisted on `OrderProduct`, but both paths additionally try to resolve the live product for nested product data.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/order/facade/OrderFacadeImpl.java:1046-1150` — private order detail/list conversion uses the deprecated populator and can fail when live product lookup is absent.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/facade/product/ProductFacadeV2Impl.java:90-115` — SKU lookup already raises `ResourceNotFoundException` when the catalog product is absent.
+
+## Root Cause Hypothesis
+
+The primary cause is that catalog product existence is treated as required for persisted cart lines and historical order presentation. Cart loading marks the whole cart obsolete instead of pruning only missing lines; the cart mapper then assumes every remaining line has a live product. Order conversion has persisted snapshot fields but performs an unnecessary live-product lookup and may fail through the conversion path. Confidence: high.
+
+## Proposed Remediation
+
+**Preferred**: Change cart population to remove only items whose SKU no longer resolves, persist the pruned line-item set, and leave an empty cart addressable rather than deleting it. Ensure all cart mappers/calculators ignore absent items and return zero totals/quantity for an empty cart. Convert missing-product additions into `ResourceNotFoundException`, yielding HTTP 404, and preserve the existing SKU lookup behavior for `GET /api/v2/product/{sku}`.
+
+Make order read conversion rely on `OrderProduct` snapshot fields for SKU, name, quantity, price, subtotal, and attributes. Live product enrichment should be optional; if the product is gone, omit only the optional nested catalog product/image and never fail order detail/list/confirmation conversion. Keep order totals and status operations based on the order aggregate, not the catalog product.
+
+**Files likely to change**:
+
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/shoppingcart/ShoppingCartServiceImpl.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/mapper/cart/ReadableShoppingCartMapper.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/shoppingCart/facade/ShoppingCartFacadeImpl.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/mapper/order/ReadableOrderProductMapper.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/populator/order/ReadableOrderProductPopulator.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/order/facade/OrderFacadeImpl.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/test/java/com/salesmanager/test/shop/integration/cart/ShoppingCartAPIIntegrationTest.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/test/java/com/salesmanager/test/shop/integration/product/ProductV2ManagementAPIIntegrationTest.java`
+- relevant order integration test under `sm-shop/src/test/java/com/salesmanager/test/shop/integration/order/`
+
+**Tests to add or update**:
+
+- Integration coverage for a cart containing deleted and surviving products: GET, PUT, multi-update, zero-product cart, recalculated quantity/subtotal/total, checkout, and 404 when adding the deleted SKU.
+- Integration coverage for deleting an ordered product and reading private detail/list and authenticated detail/list, asserting snapshot fields and unchanged totals, then changing status.
+- Integration coverage asserting deleted SKU lookup is 404 and an unrelated product remains retrievable.
+- Focused unit coverage for cart pruning and order conversion when `ProductService` returns null.
+
+## Risks & Considerations
+
+- Existing carts with no live products must remain persisted and usable for checkout; code paths that currently delete obsolete carts need to be changed consistently.
+- Removing catalog references from cart response mapping must not cause null dereferences in variant, attribute, image, shipping, or calculation logic.
+- Historical order values must not be recomputed from current catalog prices or names; only optional enrichment may use the live product.
+- Database schema changes should not be necessary; deletion must not cascade into `ORDER_PRODUCT` rows.
+- Full API integration tests may require the project database/application setup and can be expensive.
+
+## Open Questions
+
+- None blocking the remediation; the ticket specifies the required API behavior.
