+# Bug Fix: Product deletion breaks carts and historical orders
+
+- **Slug**: ticket
+- **Fixed**: 2026-11-18T21:12:00Z
+- **Assessment**: ./assessment.md
+- **Status**: applied
+
+## Summary
+
+Deleted SKUs are now removed individually from persisted carts, while empty carts remain addressable and calculate to zero. Cart additions report missing products as `ResourceNotFoundException`, and cart-total calculation ignores any stale null product references so checkout cannot charge deleted items.
+
+## Changes
+
+| File | Change | Notes |
+|------|--------|-------|
+| `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/shoppingcart/ShoppingCartServiceImpl.java` | modified | Prunes and deletes obsolete cart items instead of deleting/invalidating the whole cart; preserves empty carts. |
+| `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/order/OrderServiceImpl.java` | modified | Filters null live products during cart total calculation. |
+| `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/shoppingCart/facade/ShoppingCartFacadeImpl.java` | modified | Converts single and multi-SKU misses into 404-compatible resource-not-found errors. |
+
+## Diff Highlights
+
+- Cart retrieval now returns the original cart after removing only lines whose SKU no longer resolves.
+- Empty carts are not deleted and are passed through the normal zero-line total calculation.
+- Historical order fields remain sourced from `OrderProduct`; live product enrichment was already optional in both order conversion paths.
+
+## Tests Added or Updated
+
+- No test source files were changed; the existing integration suites were not extended because they require the application/database fixture setup.
+
+## Local Verification
+
+- Commands run: `git diff --check` → passed.
+- Commands run: `mvn -pl sm-core,sm-shop -am -DskipTests compile` → passed; all six reactor modules compiled successfully.
+- Manual checks: reviewed cart load, cart calculation, add-to-cart, order conversion, product lookup, checkout, and order status code paths.
+
+## Deviations from Assessment
+
+The assessment identified order conversion as a likely change location, but both current order conversion implementations already use persisted `OrderProduct` snapshot fields and tolerate a missing live product. No order mapper change was necessary after code inspection. The fix also added null-product filtering in `OrderServiceImpl` as a defensive checkout safeguard.
+
+## Follow-ups
+
+- Run the full API integration scenario against the configured application/database, especially deletion followed by checkout and private/authenticated order reads.
